  "note": "Montserrat is an M365 cloud font Word downloads and renders real even when\nthe fontTable names an altName for it. Its geometry is not a uniform scale\nof Liberation Sans (hmtx of Word's cached faces, 2026-09-23): lowercase\n+17.3% (+12.1% bold), capitals +5.8%, digits +4.8% (+9.5% bold), the space\nand no-break space -5.7% (+1.9% bold), Cyrillic lowercase +13.9% (+9.9%\nbold) and capitals +10%, punctuation and extended Cyrillic +11.5%, so\nper-class faces carry the adjustment (later faces win inside their\nunicode-range). Latin-1 accented capitals share the capitals face; the\naccented lowercase set is vowel-heavy and measures +10% (usage-weighted),\nso it gets a face of its own. Pitch stays the probed 1.219\n(`lineHeightFactor`).",
